#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:27
#: 16be83f2d4d14740ae8edf80adc1cdb8
msgid "Powering the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:29
#: ba1950cab12a450d89dc790ec9cdf21b
msgid "The easiest way to power the APM2.x is using a :ref:`3DR Power Module <common-3dr-power-module>` with a LiPo battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:32
#: 93046e52045042f5a222d8b3cd9237cb
msgid "To wire a power module, connect the red-and-black two wire cable on the power module to the PDB red and black two-wire. Connect the power module to the APM PM port using a 6-position cable. Connect the PDB multi-wire cable to APM Output Signal pins with the M1 wire connecting to the signal pin labeled 1, M6 and signal pin 6, etc. See the above link for additional detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:42
#: 78ea71c631414c0686212e55e6b55b45
msgid "The Power Module will not power servos and other peripherals. For more information/alternatives see :ref:`Powering the APM2 <common-powering-the-apm2>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:46
#: d031d05bcc4144a8b40e438edecfe7bf
msgid "Connect ESCs and motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:48
#: 7c2fc2b3c2644a5bbf5936c7b74b9c34
msgid ":ref:`Connecting the ESCs and Motors <connect-escs-and-motors>` explains how to set up the connections, and the motor configuration setup for each frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:52
#: a90cd46399644f1880c76b898e207686
msgid "You will need to connect motor cables to electronic speed controller (ESC) bullet connectors (each motor must connect to only one ESC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:58
#: 86dc0fbb162e4efcb6346d2c0f97b191
msgid "Connect ESC Deans connectors to Power Distribution Board (PDB) Deans connectors. Connect three-wire cables from the ESCs to the PDB signal pins according to motor number (see link above to find the motor number configuration for your frame). Connect the ESC for motor 1 to the PDB pins marked M1, motor 6's ESC to the pins marked M6, etc."
msgstr ""
